# Store and check out every file byte for byte.
#
# This repository ships dist/SHA256SUMS.txt, and a checksum is only useful if the file a
# clone receives is the file that was hashed. Git's end-of-line conversion would rewrite
# text files on checkout, differently on different platforms, so every text-file checksum
# would fail for reasons that have nothing to do with integrity. Disabling the conversion
# keeps the manifest verifiable everywhere.
#
# The cost is that text files keep the line endings they were committed with, which is the
# correct trade for a data release.
* -text
